  "assertions": 6840,
  "accepted_server_processes": 38,
  "method": "Each persistent runtime world completed three clean process boots. The next process used the exact configuration left on disk by the preceding live reload. The server registered the probe's foreign-namespace control and exposed a native registry snapshot before ServerLoadEvent STARTUP. All fixture and executable hashes were verified after shutdown.",
  "coverage": [
    "Golden control and clean vanilla restoration covered the namespace, exact keys and Bukkit descriptions of cooking/ingredient choices on the original nine Minecraft recipes producing iron ingots or diamond swords. Real player cursor, crafting callbacks and resident furnace inventory proved native conversion in both states.",
    "The exclusion startup suppressed all nine captured keys and every matching Minecraft result in the registry, while a foreign namespace and BlocksAdder's same-result crafting recipe remained usable. The selected filter persisted across live staging, foreign occupancy of a previously removed key, and plugin disable.",
    "Live single-station and empty-station settings checked all ten virtual and physical recipe definitions; six malformed configurations preserved both the previous station membership and the startup filter. Crafting, custom anvil output, custom anvil repair, ordinary vanilla repair, and stale result collection exercised a real client.",
    "Stale already-open custom crafting and anvil outputs produced no item after station deactivation and retained the inputs. Virtual anvil stale checks also verified unchanged experience levels."
  ],
